course: dictionary
lesson: 5739
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To know which one the writer means, use the context: the words and sentences around it. «The lotus leaves floated on the pond.» Ponds and floating point to the plant, so lotus means a water plant here.
explain: Now read this: «The monk sat in the lotus position beside the pond.» Sitting and monk are the clues. A lotus position is a way of sitting, not a plant, even though the pond is nearby.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence instead of the hard word. If «a way of sitting cross-legged» still makes sense in the sentence, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: A lotus is a water plant with large round leaves and big pink or white flowers.
fact: Lotus plants grow in ponds and lakes, mostly in Asia.
fact: In Buddhism and Hinduism, the lotus is a holy symbol of purity, because it grows clean out of mud.
fact: «Lotus position» means sitting cross-legged, with each foot on the opposite thigh, as in yoga and meditation.
fact: In old Greek stories, the lotus was a magic fruit that made people forget home.
exercise: «Pour water on a lotus leaf and it rolls off in silver balls.» What is the lotus here? | A way of sitting cross-legged | *A water plant with big round leaves | A magic fruit that makes people forget home
exercise: «She sat in the lotus position to calm herself before the test.» What does lotus position mean here? | A pink flower floating on a pond | A magic fruit from Greek stories | A holy river in India | *A way of sitting cross-legged, used in yoga
exercise: «In Buddhism the lotus stands for something pure rising from mud.» What does the lotus stand for? | Rain | Dirt | *Purity | Mud
test: In old Greek stories, what did eating the lotus make people do? | *Forget home | Fly over the sea | Grow wings | Sleep for a year
test: «The lotus effect» is why water rolls off a leaf and takes dirt with it. Which materials was it copied for? | Wooden chairs | Metal boats | *Self-cleaning paint and glass
exam: «The monk sat in the lotus position beside the pond.» What does lotus position mean? | A pink flower on the water | A magic fruit from Greek stories | *A way of sitting cross-legged | A leaf that repels water
